---
/**
 * FutureSection — editorial vision statement for Keel.
 *
 * Responsibility:
 * - Render a large editorial block: left-aligned on mobile, centred on tablet+.
 */
---

<section class="future-section" aria-labelledby="future-heading">
  <hr class="section-divider" />

  <div class="landing-section">
    <div class="future-block" data-reveal>
      <h2 id="future-heading" class="future-title">
        Your content should survive <span class="future-title__accent">redesigns.</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="future-body">
        AI makes redesigning your website effortless — a single prompt and your front-end is transformed. But your blog posts, portfolio images, contact form submissions, and client data should never be at risk.
      </p>
      <p class="future-body" data-reveal style="transition-delay: 120ms">
        Keel separates your content and backend from your presentation layer. Redesign as many times as you like. Your data stays permanent, versioned, and yours.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .future-section {
    background-color: var(--color-bg);
  }

  .future-block {
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    text-align: left;
    max-width: 100%;
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .future-block {
      max-width: 620px;
      text-align: center;
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .future-block {
      max-width: 760px;
    }
  }

  .future-title {
    font-size: var(--font-size-section-title);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    line-height: var(--line-height-tight);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .future-title__accent {
    position: relative;
    display: inline-block;
  }

  .future-title__accent::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: -4px;
    height: 6px;
    background-color: var(--color-chartreuse);
    border-radius: 3px;
  }

  .future-body {
    font-size: var(--font-size-section-sub);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--line-height-normal);
  }
</style>
